{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "g-23cae583fd75c7",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 1200,
			"height": 213,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Event Model\nWhat khora's events mean: identity from what happened, structure from assertions, coherence from frontiers. From K1 (#18, PR #36).\n\nColours: orange = header and Reading, purple = concepts, green = examples, red = not yet decided or a conflict, none = Decisions. *Suggestion* marks proposals not yet decided.\n\nRendered 2026-11-22 by agent:claude-opus-5-5",
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-055fe026353d0e",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "The three ideas",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 333,
			"width": 1240,
			"height": 304
		},
		{
			"id": "g-14cee7c940bfd9",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 403,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Things are identified by what happened to them**\nWhatever was asserted already has identity, so anything can be referred to, annotated or reasoned about later.\n*[[Events are the basic unit of khora]]*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-82aba7f0373abb",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 403,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**One syntax gives structure, meaning stays open**\nEvery statement is a tuple (identity, attribute, value); its attribute says what it means.\n*[[Assertions are tuples with identity]]*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-12575bc4bf13d5",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 403,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Surfaces agree by reading at the same frontier**\nA frontier is a set of events closed under their causes. Only the events relevant to a read belong in its frontier.\n*[[Events are the basic unit of khora]]*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-d20e055662edd2",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "What an event is",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 757,
			"width": 1320,
			"height": 918
		},
		{
			"id": "g-45844101ff61f8",
			"x": 1000,
			"y": 827,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Accepted action**\nA principal asked; khora accepted. Who acted and what they did.\n*In code: `AcceptedAction { by, action }`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-aeef32a5e6f8c1",
			"x": 1400,
			"y": 827,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 98,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Other kinds of event**\nNot decided yet.",
			"color": "1"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-a0cc27560c3992",
			"x": 1000,
			"y": 1465,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Event id**\nA salted hash: tamper-evident, and the newest events commit to a whole history. The salt keeps content private.\n*In code: `EventId`, canonical `Json`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-772ff2b9e8ebf9",
			"x": 1400,
			"y": 1465,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Frontier**\nA set of events with all their causes, named by its newest ones. The point a read happens at.\n*In code: `Frontier`, `FrontierCheck`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-69418d9006b811",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 1053,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Cause**\nWhat an event came from. For an action: what it read. Gives \"how did this come to be\".\n*In code: `causes`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-9f8ca76fda0499",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 1239,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Recorded time**\nClose to wall time, never backwards, after the causes.\n*In code: `Hlc`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-a672491fc8eec0",
			"x": 1200,
			"y": 1134,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Event**\nSomething that happened, kept forever with what caused it.\n*In code: `Event`, an envelope around a `Body`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-d3eca79dfaf8e4",
			"x": 1640,
			"y": 1146,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Assertions it carries**\nAn accepted assert carries one or more statements, appended together or not at all.\n*In code: `Assertion`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-5edb8f947937c8",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "What an assertion says",
			"x": 2160,
			"y": 757,
			"width": 1320,
			"height": 780
		},
		{
			"id": "g-e6a595708eb197",
			"x": 2640,
			"y": 827,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Attribute**\nA thing with identity. It carries the meaning: does a new value replace or add, what type. Definitions not built yet.\n*Well-known: `label`, `retracted` in `Basic`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-3a4eb8bc8248f3",
			"x": 2640,
			"y": 1351,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Statements about statements**\nA tuple's identity can be the identity of another tuple: a retraction, a confidence, a source, \"since 2024\".",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-75f24120240691",
			"x": 2200,
			"y": 1101,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Identity**\nThe thing the statement is about, itself the identity of an earlier assertion. No ids are invented.\n*In code: `Identity`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-68c846b5539955",
			"x": 2640,
			"y": 1113,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Assertion `(identity, attribute, value)`**\nOne statement. It has identity of its own: `e/n`, its event and its place in it.\n`(,,)` brings a new thing into being.",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-82882999890d27",
			"x": 3080,
			"y": 1101,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Value**\nA literal (text or number), or a reference to another thing's identity, which makes the statement a relationship.\n*In code: `Literal`, `Ref`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-9aff7572a798db",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Example 1: Anna creates a project, Ivan renames it",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 1795,
			"width": 1640,
			"height": 280
		},
		{
			"id": "g-23d7731727cd53",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 1865,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Anna acts**\nUnder her grant, through the projects surface, she asks to create a project called Kitchen. A request, not yet a fact.",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-a4f27dbad2bc3e",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 1865,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Event e**\n`e/0 = (,,)`: the project\n`e/1 = (e/0, name, \"Kitchen\")`\nThe project *is* `e/0`; its name, as a statement, is `e/1`.",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-70174dfa2514f5",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 1865,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Event f**, caused by e\nIvan read the project at {e}.\n`f/0 = (e/1, retracted, \"true\")`\n`f/1 = (e/0, name, \"Studio\")`",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-1f50d02c7a90be",
			"x": 1960,
			"y": 1865,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Reads**\nAt {e}: Kitchen. At {f}: Studio.\nThe history shows who renamed it and from what.",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-8ddbe42ed355fe",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Example 2: threads that do not touch each other",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 2195,
			"width": 2040,
			"height": 304
		},
		{
			"id": "g-5094f65201789d",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 2265,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Event g**: Bob issues an invoice\nAnother thread. It read nothing about the project, so it has no cause in common with f or h.",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-48a534e676a8fb",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 2265,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 80,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Event e**: the project and its name",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-f0aeb192e4a56a",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 2265,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 98,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Event f**: Ivan renames to Studio\nCauses: {e}, only what he read.",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-28b8719800bbe1",
			"x": 1960,
			"y": 2265,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Event h**: Mia renames to Atelier\nCauses: {e}. Concurrent with f, and about the same `(e/0, name)`: **a conflict**, for the attribute's merge rule.",
			"color": "1"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-44aa073b3e6afd",
			"x": 2360,
			"y": 2265,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**What g does to reads**\nNothing. A read of the project at {e} or {f} needs only those events. g is concurrent with f, but touches nothing f read, so it is not a conflict.\n*Suggestion*",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-411c155cb6606e",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Decisions it rests on",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 2619,
			"width": 840,
			"height": 556
		},
		{
			"id": "g-533a898ae41fdb",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 2689,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 122,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[An accepted action is one kind of event]]**\n*design · active*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-1d4f031a1fa928",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 2689,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 98,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Assertions are tuples with identity]]**\n*design · active*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-c7f1e3a8119e81",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 2851,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 98,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[An event carries several assertions]]**\n*design · active*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-2b441e8b0741c5",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 2851,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 122,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Event ids are salted hashes of canonical JSON]]**\n*design · active*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-2216eff4c331d7",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 3013,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 122,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[An assert's id is the identity of what it asserts]]**\n*design · active*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-2cda1b0c2c1d78",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 3013,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 98,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Events are the basic unit of khora]]**\n*design · from the Issue #21 run*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-c33964c4314ac4",
			"x": 1680,
			"y": 2619,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Reading · 2026-11-22**\n- Built and tested in K1; nothing reads assertions yet.\n- Relevance is not in the code: causes are whatever the caller passes, and nothing checks conflicts yet (K9).",
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-8203949e9e7e79",
			"x": 1680,
			"y": 2853,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 266,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Not yet decided**\n- Other kinds of event; a genesis event per log.\n- What partial tuples mean; how rejections are kept.\n- *Suggestion:* an action's causes are only what it read; a write conflicts only with concurrent events about what it read; a result reports the frontier of what it read.",
			"color": "1"
		},
		{
			"id": "spec",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 549,
			"color": "6",
			"text": "## Spec · Event Model\n\n**Purpose:** show what khora's event model *means*, as built in [[Issue #18 Event types ids and clock]] (K1): how things get identity, how structure is asserted, and how surfaces stay coherent.\n\n**Show:** the three ideas; how the concepts relate, as connections; worked examples of people acting over time, including threads that do not touch each other; each concept with its meaning, why it exists and how it is used, with its code name second; the Decisions it rests on; what is not yet decided.\n\n**Context:** the run's Design section and its Decisions; [[Events are the basic unit of khora]]; the code in `src/kernel/.../event` only to check the canvas matches it.\n\n**Judgement:** meaning before mechanics. Every claim traces to a Decision. Mark what is provisional or open.\n\n**Layout:** row 1 the ideas; row 2 the concepts as two hubs with labelled connections; rows 3 and 4 the examples; row 5 Decisions and the Reading.\n\n**Triggers:** re-render when the run's Decisions change.\n\n*Draft spec by agent:claude-opus-5-5, to be agreed with a team member.*"
		}
	],
